 "_note": "HISTORICAL POSITIONS \u2014 id -> position, UNION OVER BUILDS, never pruned.\nA player who retired in 2024 still had a position when he was added off the wire in 2023. `wire_level.js` measures what the wire PAID in 2023-25 and was reading positions from the LIVE 2026 board, so on 2026-08-13 \u2014 when the board began dropping players with no scored week in 2024/2025 \u2014 its sample silently shrank from 422 scored acquisitions to 417 and the RB level moved 7.80 -> 7.95. The direction is knowable and it is the wrong one: waiver adds who wash out of the league are exactly the LOW scorers, so pruning them biases the realized wire UPWARD, and it would have kept drifting upward on every nightly rebuild with nothing going red.\nThis file is written by build.py from the board BEFORE the activity filter runs, and MERGED rather than overwritten: a historical record may only grow.",
